Seven components
CARBOHYDRATES (yam, rice, cassava): cheap energy. PROTEINS (beans, soya, fish, eggs, milk): growth and repair — children and mothers need most. FATS/OILS (palm oil, groundnuts): concentrated energy, insulation, vitamin carriers. VITAMINS (fruits, vegetables): regulators in tiny doses — C (oranges, mango) prevents scurvy and aids iron uptake; D (sunlight, fish) builds bone with calcium; A (palm oil, liver, orange sweet potato) protects vision and immunity. MINERALS: iron (blood haemoglobin — deficiency causes ANAEMIA: fatigue, pale gums); calcium + phosphorus (bones/teeth — deficiency causes RICKETS in children); iodine (thyroid — deficiency causes GOITRE). FIBRE (vegetables, whole grains): prevents constipation and feeds gut flora. WATER: solvent, coolant (sweat), transport — 2+ litres daily in our climate. Deficiency diseases are diagnosable: kwashiorkor (protein), marasmus (total energy), night blindness (vitamin A), scurvy (vitamin C).$wdthseed$, NULL, 30, 1, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["State the seven food components and one role each","Link deficiencies (kwashiorkor, anaemia, scurvy, rickets) to missing nutrients","Judge whether a diet is balanced using energy needs"],"introduction":"A labourer needs twice the energy of an office worker; a pregnant mother needs extra iron and folate. 'Balanced diet' is not one menu — it is matching intake to need.","key_points":["Seven components + one role each","Four deficiency diagnoses","Balance depends on the person"],"references":["OpenStax Biology 2e — Chapter 41 (animal nutrition), WHO nutrition guidance (general knowledge)"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod08$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod08:top01$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.