The journey
MOUTH: teeth CHEW (mechanical — bigger surface); salivary AMYLASE starts starch → maltose (alkaline pH). OESOPHAGUS: PERISTALSIS (muscular waves) pushes the bolus down — swallowing works upside-down. STOMACH: acid (pH ~2, kills germs) + PEPSIN (protein → peptides) + churning → chyme; mucus shields the wall (failure = ulcer). SMALL INTESTINE (duodenum + ileum): the main event — PANCREATIC juice brings AMYLASE (starch → maltose), TRYPSIN (protein → peptides), LIPASE (fats → fatty acids + glycerol); BILE from the liver (stored in gall bladder) EMULSIFIES fats and neutralises acid (no enzymes in bile); intestinal enzymes finish maltose → glucose, peptides → amino acids. ILEUM: millions of VILLI (+ microvilli) absorb glucose/amino acids into blood capillaries and fatty acids/glycerol into lacteals. LARGE INTESTINE: absorbs WATER and salts; gut bacteria make vitamin K; faeces (fibre, dead cells, bacteria) egested — EGESTION removes undigested waste, EXCRETION removes metabolic waste (never confuse them).$wdthseed$, NULL, 40, 2, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["Order the gut regions and state what happens in each","Name the digestive enzymes, substrates and products","Explain how villi are adapted for absorption"],"introduction":"A pounded-yam meal becomes blood glucose in hours. Follow it down 9 metres of gut — chewed, churned, dissolved and absorbed with industrial efficiency.","key_points":["Enzyme-substrate-product triples","Bile has no enzymes","Villi routes: blood vs lacteals"],"references":["OpenStax Biology 2e — Chapter 41 (digestive system)"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod08$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod08:top01$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.content, resource_url = excluded.resource_url, duration = excluded.duration, order_number = excluded.order_number, is_published = excluded.is_published, published = excluded.published, metadata = excluded.metadata, module_id = excluded.module_id, topic_id = excluded.topic_id, course_id = excluded.course_id;
