Ventilation
INHALATION (active): external intercostal muscles contract → ribs move UP and OUT; diaphragm contracts and FLATTENS → chest volume INCREASES → pressure FALLS below outside → air rushes in. EXHALATION (passive at rest): muscles relax → ribs fall, diaphragm domes → volume DECREASES → pressure RISES → air pushed out (forced exhalation recruits internal intercostals and abdominal muscles). Air's path: nose/mouth (warmed, moistened, filtered by hairs/mucus) → trachea (C-shaped cartilage rings hold it open) → bronchi → bronchioles → ALVEOLI. Gas exchange at alveoli: O2 diffuses into blood, CO2 diffuses out — driven by concentration gradients maintained by breathing (ventilation) and heartbeat (perfusion). Adaptations: enormous surface (~100 m²), ONE-cell-thin walls, moist lining (gases dissolve), dense capillary nets.

Respiration equations
AEROBIC respiration (mitochondria, with oxygen): glucose + oxygen → carbon dioxide + water + LARGE energy (about 30 ATP per glucose). Word equation compulsory; symbol equation C6H12O6 + 6O2 → 6CO2 + 6H2O + energy earns bonus. ANAEROBIC respiration (no oxygen): in MUSCLE — glucose → lactic acid + SMALL energy (fast but weak; lactic acid causes cramp/fatigue, repaid later by deep breathing — oxygen debt); in YEAST/PLANTS — glucose → ethanol + carbon dioxide + small energy (FERMENTATION — brewing, baking, the Module 1 yeast bubbles). Smoking destroys this system: tar (carcinogen), carbon monoxide (binds haemoglobin 250x tighter than O2 — starving tissues), nicotine (addictive, narrows vessels) — causing bronchitis, emphysema (burst alveoli), lung cancer and heart disease.$wdthseed$, NULL, 40, 4, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["Describe inhalation and exhalation using ribs, diaphragm and pressure","Explain alveolar adaptations for gas exchange","Compare aerobic and anaerobic respiration with equations"],"introduction":"You breathe 20,000 times a day without thinking. Behind each breath: pressure physics, 300 million alveoli, and the respiration equation that powers Module 2's active transport.","key_points":["Pressure-volume breathing logic","Two respiration equations + ATP","Oxygen debt explanation"],"references":["OpenStax Biology 2e — Chapters 7 (cellular respiration), 34 (respiratory system)"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod08$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod08:top02$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.content, resource_url = excluded.resource_url, duration = excluded.duration, order_number = excluded.order_number, is_published = excluded.is_published, published = excluded.published, metadata = excluded.metadata, module_id = excluded.module_id, topic_id = excluded.topic_id, course_id = excluded.course_id;
