Neurones and the arc
NEURONES carry electrical impulses. SENSORY neurones run receptor → CNS (brain/spinal cord); RELAY neurones (in the CNS) connect; MOTOR neurones run CNS → effector (muscle/gland). A motor neurone has dendrites (collect signals), a long AXON wrapped in MYELIN (fatty insulation speeding impulses ~100x), and synaptic terminals. SYNAPSES (gaps between neurones) pass signals CHEMICALLY: vesicles release neurotransmitters that diffuse across and trigger the next neurone (drugs, venoms and insecticides often target synapses). REFLEX ARC order: stimulus → receptor (skin pain endings) → sensory neurone → relay neurone (spinal cord) → motor neurone → effector (arm muscle contracts) — response WITHOUT waiting for the brain (the brain is informed after, for learning). Reflexes are fast, involuntary and protective: blinking, coughing, pupil changes, knee-jerk.$wdthseed$, NULL, 30, 5, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["Label a motor neurone and state the function of its parts","Trace a reflex arc in order","Compare nervous and hormonal control"],"introduction":"Your hand jerks from a hot pot before you feel pain. That reflex — sense, decide, act in milliseconds — is your nervous system at full speed.","key_points":["Five reflex stations in order","Synapses are chemical gaps","Reflex vs voluntary routing"],"references":["OpenStax Biology 2e — Chapter 39 (nervous system)"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod08$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod08:top03$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.content, resource_url = excluded.resource_url, duration = excluded.duration, order_number = excluded.order_number, is_published = excluded.is_published, published = excluded.published, metadata = excluded.metadata, module_id = excluded.module_id, topic_id = excluded.topic_id, course_id = excluded.course_id;
