Temperature and water
HOMEOSTASIS = keeping internal conditions constant; NEGATIVE FEEDBACK = corrections opposing the change (like a thermostat). TOO HOT: hypothalamus detects warm blood → sweat glands release sweat (evaporation cools), skin arterioles VASODILATE (more blood near surface radiates heat), hair lies flat. TOO COLD: shivering (muscles respire → heat), VASOCONSTRICTION (blood kept deep — pale skin), hair stands (traps air — goosebumps), adrenaline boosts metabolism. WATER BALANCE: kidneys filter blood and reabsorb needed water (ADH hormone from the pituitary raises reabsorption when dehydrated — small, dark urine; excess water gives large, pale urine). Kidney failure is fatal without dialysis/transplant — drink water generously in our heat, and never ignore swelling or blood in urine.

Blood glucose and diabetes
The PANCREAS guards glucose. HIGH glucose (after eating): beta cells release INSULIN → liver/muscles convert glucose → GLYCOGEN (storage), cells absorb glucose → level falls. LOW glucose (exercise, hunger): alpha cells release GLUCAGON → liver converts glycogen → glucose → level rises. TYPE 1 DIABETES: beta cells destroyed (autoimmune) — no insulin; treated with INSULIN INJECTIONS for life (usually starts young). TYPE 2 DIABETES: cells resist insulin (linked to obesity, inactivity, age) — managed with diet, exercise, tablets, sometimes insulin. Uncontrolled diabetes damages eyes, kidneys, nerves and feet (amputations) — yet it is largely manageable: healthy weight, daily movement, less sugar, prescribed drugs, regular checks. Nigeria's diabetes burden is rising fast with urban diets — prevention starts on your plate.$wdthseed$, NULL, 40, 6, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["Define homeostasis and negative feedback","Explain temperature control (skin, sweat, shivering)","Explain blood-glucose control (insulin, glucagon) and diabetes"],"introduction":"Desert noon or rainy night, your core stays near 37°C and your blood glucose near normal. Stray far and enzymes fail, brains fog, lives end — homeostasis is survival.","key_points":["Negative feedback logic","Hot/cold response pairs","Insulin/glucagon + two diabetes types"],"references":["OpenStax Biology 2e — Chapters 33 (animal organisation/homeostasis), 37 (endocrine)"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod08$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod08:top03$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.content, resource_url = excluded.resource_url, duration = excluded.duration, order_number = excluded.order_number, is_published = excluded.is_published, published = excluded.published, metadata = excluded.metadata, module_id = excluded.module_id, topic_id = excluded.topic_id, course_id = excluded.course_id;
