Three graphs, one idea
A LIMITING FACTOR is the variable holding back the rate — raising it (alone) raises the rate until something else limits. LIGHT INTENSITY: rate climbs then plateaus (light no longer limits — CO2 or temperature does). CARBON DIOXIDE: same shape — enrichment boosts glasshouse crops until light/temperature cap out (note: open-field CO2 (~0.04%) almost always limits). TEMPERATURE: rises to an optimum (~25–35°C for most crops) then FALLS as enzymes denature — the asymmetric enzyme curve from Module 3. WATER rarely limits rate directly (except drought closing stomata). Measuring rate: oxygen bubbles from pondweed per minute, or CO2 uptake via sensors — with temperature, light and CO2 controlled except the one under test.$wdthseed$, NULL, 30, 2, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["Define limiting factor","Interpret rate graphs for light, CO2 and temperature","Explain two greenhouse techniques that raise yield"],"introduction":"A greenhouse farmer pumps in extra CO2 and harvests 30% more tomatoes. Same seeds, same soil — just one bottleneck removed. Limiting factors are profit.","key_points":["Three curve shapes","Plateau = another factor limits","Bottleneck-first spending"],"references":["OpenStax Biology 2e — Chapter 8 (factors affecting photosynthesis)"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod09$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod09:top01$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.content, resource_url = excluded.resource_url, duration = excluded.duration, order_number = excluded.order_number, is_published = excluded.is_published, published = excluded.published, metadata = excluded.metadata, module_id = excluded.module_id, topic_id = excluded.topic_id, course_id = excluded.course_id;
