Xylem: the water lift
ROOT HAIRS absorb soil water by OSMOSIS (Module 2) and minerals by ACTIVE TRANSPORT — their millions of extensions multiply area. Water crosses the root cortex to the XYLEM: dead, hollow, lignin-strengthened tubes running root → stem → leaf. The TRANSPIRATION STREAM pulls it up: (1) leaf cells lose water vapour through stomata (TRANSPIRATION — driven by heat, wind, dry air); (2) lost water is replaced from xylem; (3) water's COHESION (molecules gripping each other) + ADHESION (gripping walls) drags the whole column upward — one unbroken rope from roots to crown. Stomata regulate the trade: open for CO2 (photosynthesis) but losing water; closing in drought (abscisic acid triggers it) saves water but starves CO2. Wilting is lost turgor when loss beats uptake — recovered by watering, not by magic.

Phloem: the food network
PHLOEM (sieve tubes + companion cells — living, no nuclei in sieve elements) TRANSLOCATES sugars and amino acids from SOURCES (photosynthesising leaves, or storage organs in spring) to SINKS (roots, fruits, growing tips, storage tubers) — in ANY direction, unlike xylem's one-way climb. Flow is driven by pressure gradients (mass flow): sources load sugar (water follows by osmosis, raising pressure), sinks unload it (pressure falls) — sap streams from high to low pressure. Farmers exploit both systems: ring-barking (removing phloem) swells fruits above the cut; grafting joins one plant's shoot to another's roots via aligned cambia. Mineral needs: nitrates (proteins — deficiency yellows old leaves first), phosphates (roots/DNA/ATP), potassium (enzymes/stomata), magnesium (chlorophyll — deficiency yellows between veins).$wdthseed$, NULL, 35, 3, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["Trace water from soil to leaf","Explain how transpiration pulls the stream","State what phloem translocates and between which organs"],"introduction":"A 30-metre iroko lifts hundreds of litres daily with no pump, no heart, no energy bill. It runs on evaporation — physics as plumbing.","key_points":["Cohesion pulls the column","Xylem up, phloem any direction","Read deficiencies from leaves"],"references":["OpenStax Biology 2e — Chapters 30–31 (plant transport, nutrition)"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod09$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod09:top02$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.content, resource_url = excluded.resource_url, duration = excluded.duration, order_number = excluded.order_number, is_published = excluded.is