Auxin steering
TROPISM = directional growth response: PHOTOTROPISM (to light — shoots bend toward it) and GRAVITROPISM/GEOTROPISM (to gravity — roots grow down/positive, shoots grow up/negative). The hormone AUXIN (made in shoot tips) drives it: light makes auxin accumulate on the SHADED side; in SHOOTS, extra auxin SPEEDS cell elongation there — the shaded side outgrows the lit side, bending the shoot TOWARD light. In ROOTS the same extra auxin SLOWS elongation — the lower side grows less, bending the root DOWNWARD. One hormone, opposite effects by tissue — an examination favourite. Other hormones: GIBBERELLINS (stem elongation, seed germination — brewers sprout barley with them), CYTOKININS (cell division), ABSCISIC ACID (drought response — closes stomata, drops leaves), ETHENE (fruit ripening — traders ripen plantain with it).$wdthseed$, NULL, 25, 4, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["Define phototropism and gravitropism (geotropism)","Explain auxin's role in bending","Give two agricultural uses of plant hormones"],"introduction":"A seedling on your windowsill bends toward the light within days — with no eyes, muscles or brain. Hormones do the steering.","key_points":["Auxin's opposite tissue effects","Bending logic step by step","Hormone farm uses"],"references":["OpenStax Biology 2e — Chapter 30 (plant responses)"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod09$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod09:top02$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.content, resource_url = excluded.resource_url, duration = excluded.duration, order_number = excluded.order_number, is_published = excluded.is_published, published = excluded.published, metadata = excluded.metadata, module_id = excluded.module_id, topic_id = excluded.topic_id, course_id = excluded.course_id;
