Parts and light path
Follow light's journey: MIRROR/LAMP (source) → CONDENSER + IRIS DIAPHRAGM (focus and dose the light) → STAGE + CLIPS (hold the slide) → SPECIMEN → OBJECTIVE LENSES on the NOSEPIECE (x4 scanning, x10 low, x40 high — short lens = low power) → BODY TUBE → EYEPIECE (usually x10) → your eye. FOCUSING knobs: COARSE (big moves — LOW power ONLY) and FINE (small moves — all powers, the ONLY knob on high power). Total magnification = eyepiece × objective (x10 × x40 = x400). Resolution (seeing two points as separate, ~0.2 µm for light microscopes) matters more than raw magnification — empty magnification enlarges blur. Electron microscopes resolve far finer but kill specimens and cost fortunes; light microscopes show LIVING cells cheaply.

The safe routine
Memorise this drill — practical examiners watch for it. (1) Carry with TWO hands (arm + base). (2) Start on the LOWEST objective (x4/x10) with the stage DOWN. (3) Place the slide, clip it, centre the specimen over the light hole. (4) Light on, diaphragm mid-open. (5) Looking from the SIDE, raise the stage nearly to the lens (avoids crashing). (6) Look through the eyepiece, LOWER the stage slowly with COARSE focus until sharp. (7) Centre the interesting area, switch to the next objective, sharpen with FINE focus ONLY. (8) Finish: lowest objective back, stage down, light off, cover on. Golden rules: coarse knob NEVER on high power; always start low and centre before switching up; never force anything — stiffness means something is wrong.$wdthseed$, NULL, 40, 1, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["Label 8 microscope parts and state each function","Focus from low to high power without breaking slides","Calculate total magnification and estimate cell sizes"],"introduction":"A microscope turns a drop of pond water into a safari. But one wrong twist of the coarse knob cracks the slide — technique first, safari second.","key_points":["Light path order","Low-to-high drill","Magnification and field maths"],"references":["OpenStax Biology 2e — Chapter 4 (microscopy principles)"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod10$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod10:top01$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.content, resource_url = excluded.resource_url, duration = excluded.duration, order_number = excluded.order_number, is_published = excluded.is_published, published = excluded.published, metadata = excluded.metadata, module_id = excluded.module_id, topic_id = excluded.topic_id, course_id = excluded.course_id;
