Wet mounts
ONION EPIDERMIS (classic): peel the thin inner skin of an onion scale, spread FLAT on a drop of water (wrinkles ruin everything), add ONE drop of iodine stain (stains nuclei and starch brown-yellow — plant walls stay pale), lower the coverslip at 45° with a pin (hinge it down slowly — this pushes air out ahead; dropped flat, bubbles trap). BLOT excess liquid, then observe low → high. CHEEK CELLS: gentle toothpick scrape inside the cheek (your own mouth only, dispose safely), smear thin, stain with methylene blue, coverslip as above — nuclei pop blue against pale cytoplasm. RULES: thin specimens only (light must pass through); stain sparingly (over-staining blacks everything out); seal large mounts with petroleum jelly if observing long; dispose of biological waste safely and disinfect the bench.

The six drawing rules
Biological drawings are marked on: (1) SIZE — large (half a page), showing proportions; (2) LINES — sharp pencil, single continuous outlines, NO sketchy/feathered strokes, NO shading or colour (stipple dots only if texture is essential); (3) LABELS — straight ruled lines touching the structure exactly, label text at the end, never crossing lines; (4) TITLE + MAGNIFICATION — 'Onion epidermal cells (x100)' beneath, underlined; (5) HONESTY — draw ONLY what you see (no textbook additions — examiners compare with the real slide); (6) CELLS — adjacent cells share walls (single lines between, not double). Drawing magnification = drawing size ÷ real size — measure your drawn cell and divide by the known real size (or state the microscope magnification used).$wdthseed$, NULL, 35, 2, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["Prepare a stained wet mount without air bubbles","Draw cells to the six biological rules","Calculate drawing magnification correctly"],"introduction":"A great biologist draws what they see — no imagination, no artistry, just honest lines. Practical papers mark drawings harder than essays.","key_points":["45° coverslip technique","Six drawing rules","Drawing magnification formula"],"references":["OpenStax Biology 2e — Chapter 4 (studying cells)"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod10$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod10:top01$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.content, resource_url = excluded.resource_url, duration = excluded.duration, order_number = excluded.order_number, is_published = excluded.is_published, published = excluded.published, metadata = excluded.metadata, module_id = excluded.module_id, topic_id = excluded.topic_id, course_id = excluded.course_id;
