Food-test sequences
STARCH: sample + iodine → blue-black (no heat; brown-yellow = negative). REDUCING SUGAR: sample + Benedict's → HEAT in water bath 2–3 min → green/yellow/orange/brick-red by concentration (blue = negative). NON-REDUCING SUGAR: boil sample with dilute HCl → cool → neutralise with sodium hydrogencarbonate → Benedict's + heat → positive proves sucrose (the acid hydrolysed it). PROTEIN: sample + NaOH → few drops dilute CuSO4 → purple (blue = negative). FAT: shake with ethanol → pour into water → milky emulsion (or grease-spot on paper). SAFETY: goggles for heating/corrosives; water bath only (ethanol + flame = fire); tubes pointed away; tongs for hot tubes; rinse skin splashes immediately; controls (water) prove reagents are clean. Record OBSERVATION → INFERENCE separately for every tube.

Leaf-starch sequence
QUESTION: is light (or CO2, or chlorophyll) needed for photosynthesis? METHOD: (1) DESTARCH 48 h dark. (2) Set conditions: foil pattern (light test) / KOH-absorbed CO2 vs normal air (CO2 test) / variegated leaf (chlorophyll test — green vs white areas). (3) Bright light 6+ h. (4) Pluck leaf → boil in WATER (kill/soften) → boil in ETHANOL in water bath (remove chlorophyll — pale/white) → rinse → iodine. (5) Map blue-black areas against the treatment. PREDICTIONS: starch ONLY where light reached / CO2 present / chlorophyll present. CONTROLS: destarching (no old starch), plus untreated comparison leaf. CONCLUSION pattern: 'Starch formed only in [condition], therefore [factor] is necessary for photosynthesis.'$wdthseed$, NULL, 30, 4, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["Sequence every food test with safety steps","Sequence the leaf-starch test with its controls","Write methods that another student could follow"],"introduction":"Practical examinations recycle the same dozen procedures yearly. This lesson compresses them into bulletproof sequences.","key_points":["Colour triples for all five tests","Ethanol always in a water bath","Map-then-conclude pattern"],"references":["OpenStax Biology 2e — Chapters 3, 8 (detection and photosynthesis tests)"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod10$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod10:top02$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.content, resource_url = excluded.resource_url, duration = excluded.duration, order_number = excluded.order_number, is_published = excluded.is_published, published = excluded.published, metadata = excluded.metadata, module_id = excluded.module_id, topic_id = excluded.topic_id, course_id = excluded.course_id;
