Rules and responses
TEN RULES: (1) Goggles for heating, acids, alkalis, stains. (2) Tie hair, tuck ties/scarves, closed shoes, lab coat fastened. (3) NEVER taste, eat, drink or sniff directly (waft vapours). (4) Point heated tubes AWAY from people; use tongs and water baths. (5) Know exits, extinguisher, eyewash/shower, first-aid box, teacher's emergency stop. (6) Report ALL spills/breakages immediately — never hide them. (7) Dispose biologically/chemically as instructed (sharps bins, waste bottles — never sinks for chemicals). (8) Wash hands before leaving. (9) No running, no bags in aisles, stools tucked. (10) Follow the METHOD — improvisation causes accidents. EMERGENCIES: acid/alkali on skin → flood with water 10+ min, tell teacher; in eyes → eyewash immediately, keep flushing; burns → cool under running water 10+ min, no creams; cuts → pressure, raise, first aid; fire → alert, smother small flames (damp cloth/sand), evacuate for large ones; fainting → fresh air, sit/lie down.$wdthseed$, NULL, 25, 5, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["State 10 lab safety rules with reasons","Respond correctly to spills, burns, cuts and eye splashes","Read hazard symbols and choose precautions"],"introduction":"Acids blind, ethanol ignites, broken glass infects. Every rule below was written in someone's injury — learn them before you touch a bench.","key_points":["Ten rules with reasons","Splash/burn/cut/fire responses","Report-always culture"],"references":["School laboratory safety codes (general practice); CLEAPSS-style guidance principles"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod10$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod10:top03$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded