The design toolkit
VARIABLES: INDEPENDENT (what YOU change — e.g. light distance); DEPENDENT (what you MEASURE — bubbles per minute); CONTROL (what you HOLD CONSTANT — temperature, CO2, pondweed amount). FAIR TEST = one independent variable, all controls fixed. REPEATS (3+) + MEANS smooth random wobble; RANGES (5+ values of IV) reveal trends; CONTROLS (no-treatment setups) prove the IV caused the effect. VALIDITY (does it test the claim?) vs RELIABILITY (do repeats agree?): a valid method with tight repeats is trustworthy; valid-but-scattered needs more repeats; invalid-but-precise is precisely wrong. APPARATUS precision matters: measuring cylinders (±1 ml) beat beakers; thermometers beat 'warm to touch'; counting 60 seconds beats 10. SAMPLE SIZE: 30+ people for surveys, 10+ seeds per dish — small samples let chance dominate.$wdthseed$, NULL, 35, 6, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["Identify independent, dependent and control variables","Design a fair test with repeats and controls","Evaluate validity, reliability and suggest improvements"],"introduction":"Anyone can do an experiment; scientists design ones whose answers can be TRUSTED. Validity is designed in — it cannot be added afterwards.","key_points":["Variable trio","Fair-test + repeats + controls","Strength-flaws-fixes evaluation"],"references":["OpenStax Biology 2e — Chapter 1 (the scientific method)"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod10$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod10:top03$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.content, resource_url = excluded.resource_url, duration = excluded.duration, order_number = excluded.order_number, is_published = excluded.i