The non-negotiables (Modules 1–5)
MODULE 1: MRS GREN (all seven for life); cell = smallest living unit; five kingdoms by cell type/number/nutrition. MODULE 2: plant trio (wall, chloroplasts, big vacuole); prokaryote = no nucleus; diffusion (down gradient), osmosis (water + membrane), active transport (ATP, uphill); I = M × A. MODULE 3: starch/glycogen/cellulose roles; condensation out, hydrolysis in; enzyme curves (temperature cliff, pH optimum, substrate plateau); food colours — iodine blue-black (starch), Benedict's brick-red (sugar), biuret purple (protein), emulsion milky (fat). MODULE 4: PMAT + cytokinesis → 2 identical diploid; meiosis → 4 unique haploid; homologues part in anaphase I; variation = crossing over + assortment + random fertilisation. MODULE 5: five-step crosses; 3:1 and 1:2:1; ABO genotypes; X-linked males show single copies; normal parents + affected child = recessive. If any line above feels fuzzy, re-open that module NOW — Module 12 assumes mastery.$wdthseed$, NULL, 40, 1, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["State the MRS GREN set, cell trio and transport trio","Reproduce the food-test colours and enzyme curves","Solve a monohybrid and a sex-linked cross from scratch"],"introduction":"Five modules, one lesson: the facts that earn half the marks in any biology paper. Retrieve each from memory BEFORE reading on.","key_points":["Memory-first revision","Colours/curves/ratios written cold","Cross-module chaining"],"references":["OpenStax Biology 2e — Chapters 1–13 (Modules 1–5 review)"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod11$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod11:top01$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.content, re