The six commands
STATE/GIVE/NAME (1 mark each): bare facts, no explanation — 'Name the bond joining amino acids' → 'peptide bond.' Full stop. DESCRIBE: say WHAT happens (patterns, sequences) — no reasons. 'Describe the temperature curve' → 'rises to 37°C then falls steeply.' EXPLAIN: say WHY — mechanisms required. 'Explain the fall' → 'heat denatures the enzyme; the active site loses shape.' COMPARE: similarities AND differences, paired point-by-point (use 'both... whereas...' — one-sided answers halve marks). EVALUATE/DISCUSS: strengths + weaknesses + judgement with evidence. SUGGEST: apply knowledge to NEW situations — reason from first principles aloud; there is no memorised answer. MARK MATHS: 3 marks = 3 distinct points (number them); 'explain' chains need because-links; never contradict yourself (examiners mark wrong science even beside right science).

Five classic mark-losers
(1) VAGUE AGENTS — 'it goes up the plant' (WHAT goes? water? sugar? name it). (2) MISSING COMPARISONS — describing one side of a compare question. (3) UNITS ABSENT — numbers without mm/°C/min bleed marks. (4) CONTRADICTIONS — 'diffusion needs no energy because ATP drives it' scores ZERO for the point. (5) ANSWERING ANOTHER QUESTION — restating the question's data instead of explaining it. Bonus time rule: minutes ≈ marks × 1.2 — a 5-mark question gets ~6 minutes, then MOVE ON; unfinished easy marks beat perfected hard ones. Always attempt everything: blank = zero, attempt ≥ zero.$wdthseed$, NULL, 30, 3, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["Respond correctly to six command words","Write to the mark allocation (points = marks)","Avoid the five classic mark-losers"],"introduction":"Students lose 20% of marks knowing the biology but missing the COMMAND. Technique is free marks — collect them.","key_points":["Six commands, six responses","Mark maths discipline","Five losers avoided"],"references":["WOLI DAN TECH HUB original — exam technique guide (WAEC/NECO/JAMB conventions)"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod11$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod11:top02$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.content, resource_url = excluded.resource_url, duration = excluded.duration, order_number = excluded.order_number, is_published = excluded.is_published, published = excluded.published, metadata = excluded.metadata, module_id = excluded.module_id, topic_id = excluded.topic_id, course_id = excluded.course_id;
